## Exact rollback and original guard preservation

The two art sources and matching Scene GD/Python observers are current-byte/committed-byte identical to C2. Each rejected version matches its retained ignored backup and portable failed-candidate member SHA. C2→C3 has no changed production/test/tool/profile/asset bytes outside 56 generated Foundry JSONs. Therefore this is removal of the rejected presentation and its matching candidate-only observers together, not retention of failed art with weaker assertions.

Original C2 Scene 59 assertions, ten real-Node negative scenarios and twelve receipt counterexamples are exactly restored. Failed candidate's 59/14/14 source, native receipt, outputs and logs remain portable and hash-valid. Its four added Node mutations (duplicate composition, shifted root, changed actual source and foreground composition) and two receipt mutations (missing actual composition nodes and forged actual composition source) concern the abandoned composition implementation. They are not silently treated as current passes. The original current checks still cover HUD/foreground/heading/landmark/required visibility/touch/INFO errors. Exact source restoration preserves the original complete-receiver fault and **y>500** threshold; it does not replace that fall with the platform-residue control. Prior independent native failures and seven actual-data validator counterexamples in the C2 review remain unchanged source evidence, not a claim they were rerun here.

All 47 original harness check definitions are identical and every old profile membership remains. Current 52-check manifest/profiles equal C2. All 263 baseline test paths remain (275 current paths). The existing conservative removed-guard scan reports no changed-guard signals for applicable baseline→C3 test/run/config files. This supplements the prior full semantic review; it is not proof that unchanged assertion text alone guarantees semantics. Prior C2 original assertion AST/multiplicity and GUI-input/save guards are reusable because no test/tool/profile source changed since C2.

`test_change_justification` is the existing safeguard requiring coverage, actual independent review and an explanation when sensitive guards change. It is not permission to delete a useful assertion, nor a requirement to invent a new process task for an exact technical restoration. The real root `check_quality_diff --base30f` log says PASS for2969 files and explicitly still requires semantic review. This report independently checks the rollback pairing and retained applicable guards rather than treating that PASS as sufficient.

